{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KFzXhKFALFY5kBEJP6jeek","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SavPSiffAkZ23YzBwHFKtu","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/rough-workspace/opus/addendum-tests.md","content":"# Addendum: Testing Considerations\n\n*Read alongside `plan.md`. Covers test impact, test patterns, and what to verify after the monorepo migration.*\n\n---\n\n## 1. What the supplementary materials reveal\n\n### Test infrastructure overview\n\nThe test suite is organized in four tiers:\n\n| Tier | Location | Runner | Count | External deps |\n|------|----------|--------|-------|--------------|\n| Unit | `tests/unit/` | `bun:test` | 65+ files | None |\n| Integration | `tests/integration/` | `bun:test` | 10+ files | Mock LLM |\n| E2E | `tests/e2e/` | `bun:test` | 10+ files | Real API keys |\n| Cross-runtime | `tests/cross-runtime/` | `bun`/`node`/`deno` | 3+ files | None |\n\nAll tests import from `../../server/<module>` using relative paths from within the `tests/` directory. Since the `server/` directory is not moving, **no test imports need to change**.\n\n### Test runner configuration\n\n- `bunfig.toml` sets `BUN_TEST=1` environment variable for test runs\n- `package.json` defines test scripts: `test:unit`, `test:integration`, `test`, `test:e2e:init`, `test:cross-runtime:*`\n- CI uses composite action `.github/actions/run-tests/action.yml` which calls `bun test tests/unit` and `bun test tests/integration`\n\n### Test utilities\n\nKey test utilities at `tests/utils/`:\n- `sentinel-test-harness.ts` — mock LLM calls, event tracking, test workspace management\n- `mock-llm.ts` — typed mock LLM provider with configurable responses\n- `env-test-helpers.ts` — environment variable capture/restore for test isolation\n\nNone of these reference paths outside the runtime package.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Existing tests affected by the planned changes\n\n### Directly affected: None\n\nNo existing test file needs modification. The migration changes:\n1. Root `package.json` (adds `workspaces` field)\n2. Scripts in `scripts/` (path adjustments)\n3. `.gitignore` (docs artifacts)\n4. SOP document\n\nNone of these are read by tests. The `tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts` reads from `schemas/` which is unchanged. The `tests/unit/config.test.ts` reads from `server/config.ts` which is unchanged.\n\n### Potentially affected (low risk)\n\n1. **`tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts`** — Tests that generated schemas validate correctly. The schemas themselves don't change, only where they're also copied to (now `docs/public/schemas/` instead of `../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas/`). The test reads from `schemas/` which is the runtime's local copy.\n\n2. **`tests/integration/schema-zod-parity.test.ts`** — Verifies Zod schemas match JSON schemas. Same as above — reads from `schemas/`, not affected.\n\n3. **Any test reading `package.json`** — The `\"workspaces\"` field addition shouldn't affect tests that read version or package name. Verified: `tests/unit/utils.test.ts` reads `getMetadata()` which extracts `name` and `version` from `package.json` — the `workspaces` field won't interfere.\n\n### Not affected: everything else\n\nAll unit tests, integration tests, E2E tests, and cross-runtime tests operate on runtime code and mock data. They have no awareness of the docs workspace.\n\n---\n\n## 3. New tests to write\n\n### No new automated tests are strictly required\n\nThe migration is a structural change (directory layout, workspace configuration) rather than a code change. The runtime behavior is identical before and after migration.\n\n### Recommended manual verification checklist\n\nAfter migration, verify by hand (or in a CI validation step):\n\n```bash\n# 1. Workspace installs correctly\nbun install\n# Expected: success, single bun.lock at root, docs/node_modules linked\n\n# 2. Runtime tests still pass\nbun run test:unit\nbun run test:integration\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\n\n# 3. Schema generation writes to both locations\nbun run generate-schemas\nls schemas/hank-file.schema.json\nls docs/public/schemas/hank-file.schema.json\n\n# 4. Runtime build works\nbun run build\nls dist/index.js\n\n# 5. Docs build works\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n\n# 6. npm pack excludes docs\nnpm pack --dry-run\n# Expected: docs/ NOT in the file list\n\n# 7. Sync dry-run strips docs correctly (requires git history)\nbun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version <version> --use-head\n# Expected: \"Correctly removed: docs\" in verification output\n```\n\n### Optional: Add a workspace smoke test\n\nIf desired, a lightweight test could be added to verify the monorepo structure is consistent:\n\n```typescript\n// tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts\nimport { describe, test, expect } from \"bun:test\";\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\n\ndescribe(\"monorepo structure\", () => {\n  const ROOT = path.resolve(import.meta.dir, \"../..\");\n\n  test(\"root package.json declares docs workspace\", () => {\n    const pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    expect(pkg.workspaces).toContain(\"docs\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs workspace has package.json\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"package.json\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs schemas directory exists\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"public\", \"schemas\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\nThis is lightweight and validates the structural invariant. Optional — only add if the team wants structural tests.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Edge cases to cover\n\n### 4.1: `bun install --frozen-lockfile` in CI\n\nAfter migration, the CI composite action (`.github/actions/setup-environment/action.yml:34`) runs:\n```bash\nbun install --frozen-lockfile\n```\n\nThis will fail if the `bun.lock` at root doesn't include the docs workspace's dependencies. **The `bun.lock` must be regenerated and committed as part of the migration.**\n\n### 4.2: The docs workspace's `devDependencies` in the root lockfile\n\nThe docs workspace has these dependencies that the runtime doesn't:\n- `next` ^15.0.0\n- `nextra` ^4.0.0\n- `nextra-theme-docs` ^4.0.0\n- `react` ^19.0.0\n- `react-dom` ^19.0.0\n- `@vercel/analytics` ^1.6.1\n- `posthog-js` ^1.347.2\n- `pagefind` ^1.3.0\n\nThese will be added to the root `bun.lock`. They should NOT conflict with the runtime's dependencies. The runtime doesn't use React or Next.js. The only shared dependency is `typescript` — both packages use it but can have independent versions.\n\n### 4.3: `npm publish` from root\n\nThe `release.yml` runs `npm publish` from the repo root. The `\"files\"` field in `package.json`:\n```json\n\"files\": [\"dist\", \"shims\", \"schemas\"]\n```\n\nThis is an allowlist — `docs/` won't be included. Verify with `npm pack --dry-run` that the published tarball doesn't include docs workspace files.\n\n### 4.4: Build executable with workspace\n\n`build-executable.ts` uses `ENTRY_POINT = \"server/index.ts\"` and builds from root. Bun's build should resolve the entry point the same way with or without workspaces. Verify: `bun scripts/build-executable.ts` produces a working binary.\n\n### 4.5: Cross-runtime tests\n\n`scripts/run-cross-runtime-tests.ts` resolves `testsDir` from `import.meta.dirname`. This path doesn't change. Cross-runtime tests import from `../../server/` which doesn't change. Should work without modification.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Test patterns and conventions to follow\n\nIf adding any new tests (e.g., the optional monorepo structure test):\n\n1. **Location**: `tests/unit/` for unit tests, `tests/integration/` for integration\n2. **Import style**: `import { ... } from \"bun:test\"` for test framework, `import * as fs from \"node:fs\"` for Node APIs\n3. **Relative imports**: `../../server/<module>` from test files\n4. **Cleanup**: Create temp directories, clean up in `afterEach`/`afterAll`\n5. **No global state**: Each test should be independent\n6. **Biome compliance**: Tests in `tests/unit/` and `tests/e2e/` are covered by Biome linting\n\n---\n\n## 6. Conflicts or inconsistencies\n\n**None identified.** The plan and test infrastructure are consistent. The migration doesn't touch any runtime code, so all existing tests should pass without modification.\n\nThe only \"inconsistency\" worth noting: the `generate-schemas.ts` script currently silently skips writing to docs if the path doesn't exist (`docsAvailable` check). After migration, this path will always exist, so the `docsAvailable` check becomes redundant. The plan recommends keeping the check (defensive) rather than removing it (premature cleanup).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Risks\n\n1. **Dependency hoisting conflicts**: Bun workspaces hoists dependencies. If the runtime and docs have conflicting versions of a shared transitive dependency, the hoist could cause issues. This is unlikely — the two packages have almost entirely different dependency trees (server-side Bun tools vs. React/Next.js).\n\n2. **CI time increase**: CI now installs docs dependencies even when only runtime code changed. This adds maybe 10-20 seconds to `bun install`. Not worth optimizing initially. Path filtering in CI can be added later.\n\n3. **Lockfile churn**: The unified `bun.lock` will see more frequent changes because it covers both workspaces. Docs dependency updates will modify the lockfile even when no runtime code is affected. This is normal for monorepos and a minor inconvenience.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4485,"cache_read_input_tokens":95155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4485},"output_tokens":2661,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f6abf3a-0b5f-4251-a578-7f2d66ac9b9a","uuid":"5ee8dd71-5613-4c40-97c6-28b7c0edd585","timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:19:10.436Z"}
