rate-schemas.ts)\n├── styles/                         Global CSS\n├── next.config.mjs                 Nextra + Next.js config\n├── package.json                    hankweave-docs v2.0.0\n├── tsconfig.json                   ES2020, bundler moduleResolution\n└── vercel.json                     Framework: nextjs, bun install/build\n```\n\n### Key observations from docs content\n\n1. **No runtime imports**: The docs site doesn't import TypeScript modules from the runtime. It references hankweave as a CLI tool (`npx hankweave`, `bunx hankweave`) but doesn't use it as a library dependency.\n\n2. **Schema hosting**: The `public/schemas/` directory hosts JSON schemas generated by the runtime's `generate-schemas.ts`. This is the only data flow from runtime to docs. The schemas are served as static files — they're referenced from the docs pages via URLs like `/schemas/hank-file.schema.json`.\n\n3. **Layout references public repo**: `app/layout.tsx:64` links to `https://github.com/SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` as the project link. This doesn't change — the public mirror continues to be the user-facing repo.\n\n4. **PostHog analytics**: The docs site uses PostHog for analytics (`app/posthog-provider.tsx`). This is a client-side integration and doesn't affect the migration.\n\n5. **Pagefind search**: The `postbuild` script runs `pagefind --site .next/server/app --output-path public/_pagefind` to generate a search index. This runs relative to the docs workspace directory and will work in the monorepo.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Documentation that needs updating\n\n### 2.1: `standard-operating-procedures.md` — Repository Structure (Section 1)\n\n**File**: `source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md:10-30`\n\nUpdate the directory tree to include `docs/`:\n\n```markdown\n## 1. Repository Structure\n\n```\nhankweave-dev/              ← private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n├── server/                 ← runtime source code (TypeScript, Bun)\n├── scripts/                ← build, release, sync, and dev tooling\n├── tests/                  ← unit, integration, e2e, cross-runtime\n├── schemas/                ← generated JSON schemas (from Zod)\n├── shims/                  ← agent harness adapters\n├── docs/                   ← documentation site workspace (Next.js + Nextra)\n│   ├── app/                ← Next.js app directory\n│   ├── content/            ← MDX documentation pages\n│   ├── components/         ← custom React components\n│   ├── public/             ← static assets + generated schemas\n│   └── package.json        ← hankweave-docs workspace\n├── learning/               ← example hanks and guides (ships to public)\n├── intermediates/          ← planning docs (internal only)\n├── external-docs/          ← SDK reference docs for agent context (internal only)\n├── public-release-files/   ← files overlaid onto public repo during sync\n├── assets/                 ← images, demo GIFs\n├── .github/                ← CI workflows and composite actions\n├── CHANGELOG.md            ← Keep a Changelog format\n├── CONTRIBUTING.md         ← branch model and PR guidelines (internal only)\n└── package.json            ← @southbridgeai/hankweave + workspace root\n```\n\nThere is a separate public repo at `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` which receives sanitized snapshots via the sync workflow. It publishes the public `hankweave` npm package.\n\nThe documentation site (`docs/`) deploys to Vercel from this repo. It is a Bun workspace but does not have a workspace dependency on the runtime package.\n```\n\n### 2.2: `standard-operating-procedures.md` — Strip List (Section 1)\n\n**File**: `source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md:34-36`\n\nAdd `docs/` to the \"What gets stripped\" list:\n\n```markdown\n### What gets stripped before public release\n\nThe sync process (`scripts/sync-public.ts`) removes internal-only content:\n\n- **Directories**: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`, `docs/`\n```\n\n### 2.3: `standard-operating-procedures.md` — Key Files Reference (Section 9)\n\n**File**: `source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md:337-354`\n\nAdd docs workspace entry:\n\n```markdown\n| `docs/package.json`                    | Documentation site workspace (hankweave-docs)                                 |\n| `docs/content/`                        | MDX documentation pages (concepts, guides, reference)                         |\n```\n\n### 2.4: `standard-operating-procedures.md` — Development Workflow (Section 3)\n\nConsider adding a note about the docs workspace:\n\n```markdown\n### Documentation site\n\nThe documentation site is a Bun workspace at `docs/`. To build it locally:\n\n```bash\ncd docs && bun run dev    # Development server (hot reload)\ncd docs && bun run build  # Production build\n```\n\nChanges to docs pages (`docs/content/**/*.mdx`) are deployed automatically via Vercel when pushed to the configured branch.\n\nWhen generating schemas, they are automatically written to both `schemas/` (for the npm package) and `docs/public/schemas/` (for the docs site):\n\n```bash\nbun run generate-schemas\n```\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Documentation that should NOT be updated\n\n### User-facing docs (`docs/content/**/*.mdx`)\n\nThe user-facing documentation covers:\n- **Concepts**: Codons, Hanks, Rigs, Loops, Checkpoints, Sentinels, Execution Flow\n- **Guides**: Getting Started, Building Hanks, Testing, Debugging, Docker\n- **Reference**: CLI, Configuration, API Keys, Protocol, Event Journal\n\nNone of these reference the repository structure. They document Hankweave as a product/CLI tool. The monorepo migration is an internal change that doesn't affect users.\n\n### Public README (`public-release-files/README.md`)\n\nThis file is overlaid onto the public mirror (`hankweave-runtime`). It describes installation, usage, and links to documentation. The monorepo structure is invisible to public users.\n\n### `CHANGELOG.md`\n\nThe changelog documents user-facing changes. The monorepo migration is an infrastructure change. It could be mentioned under an \"Internal\" or \"Changed\" section if desired, but it's not user-facing:\n\n```markdown\n## [Unreleased]\n\n### Changed\n\n- **Monorepo migration** — Consolidated documentation site into the development repository as a Bun workspace. No changes to runtime behavior or public-facing interfaces.\n```\n\nThis is optional.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Vercel deployment details\n\n### Current state\n\nThe docs site currently deploys from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs`. Vercel is configured to:\n1. Connect to the `hankweave-docs` GitHub repo\n2. Build with `bun run build` (as specified in `vercel.json`)\n3. Use Next.js framework detection\n4. Deploy to the configured domain\n\n### Required changes\n\n**Step 1: Connect Vercel to the monorepo**\n\nIn the Vercel dashboard:\n1. Go to the hankweave-docs project settings\n2. Under \"Git\" → \"Connected Git Repository\"\n3. Change from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`\n4. Set \"Root Directory\" to `docs`\n\n**Step 2: Configure Ignored Build Step (optional but recommended)**\n\nTo prevent unnecessary docs rebuilds when only runtime code changes:\n1. Go to Settings → General → \"Ignored Build Step\"\n2. Set to: `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/`\n\nThis tells Vercel to skip the build if no files under `docs/` have changed.\n\n**Step 3: Verify `vercel.json` is at the right level**\n\nThe `vercel.json` currently in `nextra-site/` (which becomes `docs/`) contains:\n```json\n{\n  \"framework\": \"nextjs\",\n  \"installCommand\": \"bun install\",\n  \"buildCommand\": \"bun run build\"\n}\n```\n\nWhen Vercel's root directory is set to `docs`, it will look for `vercel.json` in `docs/vercel.json`. This is correct.\n\n**Important**: The `installCommand: \"bun install\"` in `vercel.json` runs from `docs/`, but because it's part of a Bun workspace, Bun will install the root lockfile and all workspace dependencies. This should work, but verify:\n- Vercel may need the root `package.json` accessible to resolve the workspace configuration\n- If Vercel only mounts the `docs/` subdirectory, workspace resolution might fail\n\n**Fallback**: If workspace resolution fails in Vercel, change the root directory to `/` (repo root) and update `buildCommand` to `cd docs && bun run build`. The `installCommand` stays as `bun install` (at root).\n\n**Step 4: Verify branch configuration**\n\nVercel should deploy from the branch where docs changes land. Currently this is likely `main` or `master` of `hankweave-docs`. In the monorepo, the branches are `develop` and `release/alpha`. Configure Vercel to:\n- Production deployment: `release/alpha` (or `develop`, depending on preference)\n- Preview deployments: PRs targeting `develop`\n\n### Things that don't change\n\n- The `next.config.mjs` stays the same\n- The `postbuild` pagefind step stays the same\n- The PostHog integration stays the same\n- The domain/DNS stays the same\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cross-repo schema flow after migration\n\n### Before migration\n\n```\nhankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts\n  → writes to hankweave/schemas/                    (local, always works)\n  → writes to ../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas/  (sibling repo, works only if checked out)\n```\n\n### After migration\n\n```\nhankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts\n  → writes to hankweave/schemas/                    (local, always works)\n  → writes to hankweave/docs/public/schemas/         (same repo, always works)\n```\n\nThe `docsAvailable` check in `generate-schemas.ts` becomes permanently true (the `docs/` directory is always present in the monorepo). The check should be kept for safety but will never evaluate to false in normal operation.\n\n### Release flow for schemas\n\n1. Developer runs `bun run generate-schemas` (or it runs automatically during release)\n2. Schemas are written to both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`\n3. Both locations are committed together\n4. When the runtime is synced to public, `schemas/` goes with it\n5. When docs deploy to Vercel, `docs/public/schemas/` goes with it\n6. Both consumers always have the latest schemas — no coordination needed\n\nThis is the primary benefit of the monorepo: what was previously a fragile cross-repo file write is now a simple intra-repo operation that's always consistent.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implications and risks from docs review\n\n### 6.1: `hankweave-docs` repo archival\n\nAfter the monorepo migration, the `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` repo becomes orphaned. It should be:\n1. Archived (read-only) on GitHub\n2. README updated to say \"This repo has been merged into SouthBridgeAI/hankweave\"\n3. Vercel disconnected (after the new Vercel connection is verified)\n\n### 6.2: The `notes/` and `plan/` directories\n\nThe docs repo has `hankweave-docs/notes/` and `hankweave-docs/plan/` directories outside `nextra-site/`. These are internal planning documents. Options:\n- **Discard**: They're historical and won't be needed going forward\n- **Archive**: Copy them into `intermediates/` as a numbered entry (e.g., `intermediates/docs-migration/legacy-notes/`)\n- **Include in docs/**: Keep them at `docs/notes/` and `docs/plan/` (they won't be built by Next.js since they're not in `content/` or `app/`)\n\nRecommendation: Discard. If the team wants them preserved, archive in `intermediates/`.\n\n### 6.3: Build environment variable\n\nThe `vercel.json` contains:\n```json\n{\n  \"build\": {\n    \"env\": {\n      \"DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969\": \"1\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis environment variable is specific to the docs Vercel build and will continue to work in the same `vercel.json` at `docs/vercel.json`. No change needed, but worth noting for awareness.\n\n### 6.4: No new docs pages needed\n\nThe monorepo migration is purely internal infrastructure. No new user-facing documentation pages are needed. The guides, concepts, and reference pages all document Hankweave's behavior and interface, not its repository layout.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Assumptions revisited after docs review\n\n### Assumption: \"The docs have no dependency on the runtime package\"\n\n**Confirmed.** After reviewing the full docs source (layout.tsx, page components, MDX content), there are zero imports from `@southbridgeai/hankweave` or any runtime module. The only data flow is the schema JSON files generated by the runtime's script.\n\n### Assumption: \"Vercel can build the docs from a monorepo subdirectory\"\n\n**Mostly confirmed, with a caveat.** Vercel supports monorepos with root directory configuration. However, Bun workspaces require the root `package.json` to be accessible for workspace resolution. If Vercel only mounts the subdirectory, `bun install` in `docs/` might not find the root `package.json` and might treat `docs/` as a standalone project (which would still work — just without workspace hoisting).\n\n**Mitigation**: If this is an issue, set Vercel root directory to `/` and update the build command to `cd docs && bun run build`.\n\n### Assumption: \"No shared development dependencies worth consolidating\"\n\n**Confirmed.** The only shared dependency is `typescript`. The runtime uses Bun-specific APIs and `bun-types`, while the docs use React, Next.js, and Nextra. There's no benefit to Bun catalogs or shared configs at this point.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:20:44.026Z"}
