{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UbbhqiX7C3vvEzAwtvHtJG","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Plan: Migrate Hankweave to Monorepo\n     2→\n     3→## a. The Main Task\n     4→\n     5→Consolidate the `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave` (runtime) and `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` (documentation site) repositories into a single monorepo using Bun workspaces. The runtime package stays at the repository root; the docs site moves in as a workspace at `docs/`. The existing CI/CD pipelines, release process, and public sync workflow continue to function with minimal changes.\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## b. Information Available\n    10→\n    11→### Sources that informed this plan\n    12→\n    13→1. **Task specification** — `plan/task.md` (the task description, open questions, and research)\n    14→2. **Background research** — `plan/background/background.md` (Bun workspace docs, Turborepo evaluation, git subtree options)\n    15→3. **Full source code** — Read every config, script, workflow, and representative server/test files from both repos\n    16→4. **SOP document** — `source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md` (branch model, release process, AI agent policy)\n    17→\n    18→### What I could see\n    19→\n    20→- Full directory structure and file contents of both `source/hankweave/` and `source/hankweave-docs/`\n    21→- All CI workflows, composite actions, and build/release/sync scripts\n    22→- Test infrastructure (patterns, paths, utilities, config fixtures)\n    23→- Both `package.json` files, `tsconfig.json` files, `biome.json`, `bunfig.toml`\n    24→- The docs Nextra/Next.js setup including `vercel.json`, `next.config.mjs`, `app/`, `content/`\n    25→\n    26→### What I could NOT see\n    27→\n    28→- The actual `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` (public mirror) repo — only references to it in scripts and workflows\n    29→- Vercel project settings (the current \"Root Directory\" config for docs deployment)\n    30→- GitHub repo settings (branch protection rules, secrets configuration)\n    31→- Linear project (no ticket ID was provided)\n    32→- Whether there are any other repositories or tools the task spec's \"related packages/tools\" refers to beyond what's in the source snapshot\n    33→\n    34→### Assumptions made\n    35→\n    36→1. The `hankweave-docs` repo has no significant git history worth preserving (the task says \"nice to have\" for history)\n    37→2. The public mirror (`hankweave-runtime`) continues to exist as a separate repo — this migration consolidates the two **private development** repos\n    38→3. The docs site continues to deploy to Vercel from the same repo (now a monorepo)\n    39→4. No Turborepo or other task orchestration is needed for two packages\n    40→\n    41→---\n    42→\n    43→## c. Sources and Related Things\n    44→\n    45→### Original tickets/tasks\n    46→\n    47→- Task description: `plan/task.md`\n    48→- No Linear ticket ID provided\n    49→\n    50→### Code references\n    51→\n    52→| File | Line(s) | Relevance |\n    53→|------|---------|-----------|\n    54→| `source/hankweave/package.json` | Full | Root package.json — needs `workspaces` field added |\n    55→| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/package.json` | Full | Docs package.json — moves to `docs/package.json` |\n    56→| `source/hankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts` | 24-32 | The only cross-repo code dependency; path to docs schemas dir |\n    57→| `source/hankweave/scripts/sync-public.ts` | 28-44 | STRIP_DIRS/STRIP_FILES — needs `docs` added to strip list |\n    58→| `source/hankweave/scripts/release.ts` | 54-60 | INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP — needs `docs/` added |\n    59→| `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/ci.yml` | Full | CI workflow — minimal changes needed |\n    60→| `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/release.yml` | Full | Release workflow — minimal changes |\n    61→| `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/sync-public.yml` | Full | Sync workflow — minimal changes |\n    62→| `source/hankweave/.github/actions/setup-environment/action.yml` | Full | Composite action — `bun install` already handles workspaces |\n    63→| `source/hankweave/biome.json` | Full | Linting scope — currently only covers runtime files |\n    64→| `source/hankweave/bunfig.toml` | Full | Bun config — no changes needed |\n    65→| `source/hankweave/tsconfig.json` | Full | Runtime TypeScript config — stays as-is |\n    66→| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/tsconfig.json` | Full | Docs TypeScript config — stays as-is in new location |\n    67→| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/vercel.json` | Full | Vercel config — stays in docs workspace |\n    68→| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/next.config.mjs` | Full | Next.js config — no changes |\n    69→| `source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md` | 10-30, 34-36 | Repository structure section — needs update |\n    70→| `source/hankweave/.gitignore` | Full | May need additions for docs build artifacts |\n    71→| `source/hankweave/scripts/test-sync-local.ts` | 159-175 | Verification list — needs `docs` added |\n    72→\n    73→### Research sources\n    74→\n    75→- [Bun Workspaces](https://bun.sh/docs/install/workspaces) — native workspace support via `package.json` `workspaces` field\n    76→- [Bun Catalogs](https://bun.sh/docs/install/catalogs) — optional shared dependency versioning (not needed initially)\n    77→- [git subtree merges](https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/using-git/about-git-subtree-merges) — for preserving docs repo history\n    78→\n    79→---\n    80→\n    81→## d. Conventions and Patterns\n    82→\n    83→### Observed code conventions\n    84→\n    85→1. **Scripts are TypeScript** — all build/release/sync scripts are `.ts` files run with `bun`\n    86→2. **Relative paths from `import.meta.dir`** — scripts use `path.join(import.meta.dir, \"..\")` to resolve project root\n    87→3. **`Bun.spawn` for shell commands** — scripts use `Bun.spawn([\"sh\", \"-c\", cmd])` rather than Node's `child_process`\n    88→4. **Two-space indent, 100-char line width** — enforced by Biome\n    89→5. **LF line endings** — enforced by `.gitattributes`\n    90→6. **No shared state between packages** — docs don't import from runtime; only schema files are copied\n    91→7. **Strip lists are explicit** — both `sync-public.ts` and `release.ts` maintain explicit lists of files/dirs to remove\n    92→\n    93→### Patterns to follow\n    94→\n    95→- Add `docs` to existing strip lists rather than creating new mechanisms\n    96→- Keep the root `package.json` as the runtime's package.json (add `workspaces` field only)\n    97→- Don't introduce Turborepo or other tooling — Bun workspaces is sufficient\n    98→- Keep separate `tsconfig.json` per workspace (they have incompatible settings)\n    99→- Don't introduce workspace dependencies (`workspace:*`) between docs and runtime — the schema copy is a script-level operation\n   100→\n   101→### Patterns to avoid\n   102→\n   103→- Don't move the runtime into a subdirectory (would break dozens of paths)\n   104→- Don't create a shared `tsconfig.base.json` (the two configs are too different)\n   105→- Don't add a `bun` workspace filter to CI scripts (just let everything install and run from root)\n   106→\n   107→---\n   108→\n   109→## e. Decision Points and Judgement Calls\n   110→\n   111→### Decision 1: Keep the runtime at the repo root\n   112→\n   113→**Chosen**: The runtime stays at root. The docs site moves into `docs/`.\n   114→\n   115→**Reasoning**: The runtime has 6 scripts, 3 CI workflows, 3 composite actions, build/release/sync pipelines, and extensive relative path usage. Moving it into a subdirectory would require changing every one of these. The docs site has no CI of its own (Vercel builds it), no complex scripts, and one `package.json`. Moving the docs in is a fraction of the work.\n   116→\n   117→**Trade-off**: The root `package.json` serves dual purpose as both workspace root and runtime package. This is a recognized Bun workspace pattern and works correctly — the root package is an \"implicit workspace member\" by default.\n   118→\n   119→**Impact**: Minimal disruption to existing workflows. The main changes are:\n   120→- Adding `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` to root `package.json`\n   121→- Updating 2-3 file paths in scripts\n   122→- Adding `docs` to strip lists\n   123→\n   124→### Decision 2: Flatten the docs repo structure\n   125→\n   126→**Chosen**: Move `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/*` contents directly into `docs/` (not `docs/nextra-site/`).\n   127→\n   128→**Reasoning**: The `nextra-site/` wrapper exists because the docs repo has a root with README, notes, and plan directories. In the monorepo, these don't need a separate layer. The `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `next.config.mjs`, and all source files go directly in `docs/`.\n   129→\n   130→**Alternative considered**: Keeping `docs/nextra-site/` as-is. This preserves the original structure but adds an unnecessary level of nesting. It also means `\"workspaces\": [\"docs/nextra-site\"]` which is less clean.\n   131→\n   132→**What to do with `hankweave-docs/` non-nextra files**: The `README.md` at docs repo root, `notes/`, and `plan/` directories are development artifacts. They can either:\n   133→- Be discarded (they're internal planning docs)\n   134→- Be moved to an `intermediates/` entry documenting the docs site\n   135→- Be kept at `docs/` level alongside the nextra files\n   136→\n   137→**Recommendation**: Discard `notes/` and `plan/` (they're historical planning docs). Keep the `README.md` as `docs/README.md` if desired, but it's not required.\n   138→\n   139→### Decision 3: Don't use `workspace:*` dependencies\n   140→\n   141→**Chosen**: No workspace dependency between docs and runtime.\n   142→\n   143→**Reasoning**: The docs site doesn't import from the runtime. The only data flow is schema JSON files copied by `generate-schemas.ts`. This is a script-level file copy, not a package dependency. Adding a `workspace:*` dependency would incorrectly suggest the docs depend on the runtime as a package.\n   144→\n   145→**When to revisit**: If the docs site ever needs to import TypeScript types or utilities from the runtime (e.g., for auto-generated API reference), add `workspace:*` at that point.\n   146→\n   147→### Decision 4: Convert the existing hankweave repo, don't create new\n   148→\n   149→**Chosen**: Modify `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave` in-place to become the monorepo.\n   150→\n   151→**Reasoning**: All CI workflows, GitHub secrets, branch protection rules, Linear integration, and team permissions are already configured on this repo. Creating a new repo would require reconfiguring everything. The existing git history stays intact. The docs files are brought in via a merge commit (or `git subtree add` if history preservation is desired).\n   152→\n   153→**Impact**: No disruption to existing CI/CD. No need to update secrets, protections, or integrations.\n   154→\n   155→### Decision 5: No Turborepo\n   156→\n   157→**Chosen**: Use Bun workspaces alone, no Turborepo.\n   158→\n   159→**Reasoning**: Two packages don't need task orchestration or caching. The runtime builds and tests independently. The docs site builds independently on Vercel. There's no dependency chain requiring `^build` semantics. Adding Turborepo would increase complexity with no clear benefit.\n   160→\n   161→**When to revisit**: If more packages are added (e.g., a shared types package, a CLI package), or if CI times become a problem and caching would help.\n   162→\n   163→### Decision 6: Single lockfile at root\n   164→\n   165→**Chosen**: One `bun.lock` at the repo root, replacing both existing lockfiles.\n   166→\n   167→**Reasoning**: Bun workspaces uses a single root lockfile. Both workspace packages' dependencies are resolved and locked together. This is how Bun workspaces work by default — there's no option for per-workspace lockfiles.\n   168→\n   169→**Impact**: The `bun.lock` from `hankweave` and the `bun.lock` from `hankweave-docs/nextra-site` are both replaced by a regenerated root `bun.lock`. The first `bun install` after migration will generate this.\n   170→\n   171→### Over/under engineering line\n   172→\n   173→- **Under**: Not adding path filtering to CI (docs changes trigger runtime tests). Acceptable for now — CI runs are fast and infrequent enough.\n   174→- **Under**: Not using Bun catalogs for shared TypeScript version. Acceptable — the projects only share TypeScript and it's fine to have independent versions.\n   175→- **Over**: Adding Turborepo, shared configs, workspace link scripts, or monorepo-specific CI tooling. Not needed for two packages.\n   176→- **Right level**: Adding `docs` to strip lists, updating one path in `generate-schemas.ts`, updating the SOP doc. Minimal changes that make the monorepo work.\n   177→\n   178→---\n   179→\n   180→## f. The Actual Implementation Plan\n   181→\n   182→### Phase 0: Preparation\n   183→\n   184→**Step 0.1: Create a feature branch**\n   185→```bash\n   186→git checkout develop\n   187→git pull origin develop\n   188→git checkout -b hrishi/monorepo-migration  # or similar\n   189→```\n   190→\n   191→**Step 0.2: Verify clean state**\n   192→- Ensure all tests pass: `bun run test:unit`, `bun run lint`, `bun run tc`\n   193→- Ensure working directory is clean: `git status`\n   194→\n   195→### Phase 1: Bring docs into the repo\n   196→\n   197→**Step 1.1: Create the `docs/` directory**\n   198→\n   199→Copy the contents of `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/` at the runtime repo root.\n   200→\n   201→Files to copy from `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/`:\n   202→```\n   203→app/\n   204→components/\n   205→content/\n   206→public/\n   207→styles/\n   208→bun.lock           (will be removed later — root lockfile takes over)\n   209→mdx-components.tsx\n   210→next-env.d.ts\n   211→next.config.mjs\n   212→package.json\n   213→tsconfig.json\n   214→vercel.json\n   215→```\n   216→\n   217→Files from `hankweave-docs/` root to optionally include:\n   218→```\n   219→.gitignore          → merge relevant rules into root .gitignore\n   220→README.md           → can include as docs/README.md (internal docs readme)\n   221→```\n   222→\n   223→Files to NOT copy:\n   224→```\n   225→notes/              → historical planning docs, discard\n   226→plan/               → historical planning docs, discard\n   227→```\n   228→\n   229→**Step 1.2: Add workspace configuration to root `package.json`**\n   230→\n   231→Modify `source/hankweave/package.json` — add `workspaces` field:\n   232→\n   233→```json\n   234→{\n   235→  \"name\": \"@southbridgeai/hankweave\",\n   236→  \"version\": \"0.5.6\",\n   237→  \"workspaces\": [\"docs\"],\n   238→  ...\n   239→}\n   240→```\n   241→\n   242→**Step 1.3: Delete the docs-side `bun.lock`**\n   243→\n   244→Remove `docs/bun.lock` (the old `nextra-site/bun.lock`). The root lockfile will manage all dependencies.\n   245→\n   246→**Step 1.4: Run `bun install`**\n   247→\n   248→From the repo root, run `bun install`. This:\n   249→- Resolves dependencies for both workspaces\n   250→- Generates a new unified `bun.lock` at root\n   251→- Creates a single `node_modules/` tree\n   252→\n   253→Verify: `docs/node_modules` should be a symlink or the workspace should be hoisted.\n   254→\n   255→**Step 1.5: Verify docs build locally**\n   256→\n   257→```bash\n   258→cd docs && bun run build\n   259→```\n   260→\n   261→Verify the Next.js build succeeds. If there are issues with module resolution, they'll surface here.\n   262→\n   263→### Phase 2: Update cross-repo references\n   264→\n   265→**Step 2.1: Update `scripts/generate-schemas.ts`**\n   266→\n   267→Change the `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path from:\n   268→```typescript\n   269→const DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR = path.join(\n   270→  import.meta.dir,\n   271→  \"..\",\n   272→  \"..\",\n   273→  \"hankweave-docs\",\n   274→  \"nextra-site\",\n   275→  \"public\",\n   276→  \"schemas\",\n   277→);\n   278→```\n   279→\n   280→To:\n   281→```typescript\n   282→const DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR = path.join(\n   283→  import.meta.dir,\n   284→  \"..\",\n   285→  \"docs\",\n   286→  \"public\",\n   287→  \"schemas\",\n   288→);\n   289→```\n   290→\n   291→This is the only code change needed to formalize the cross-package dependency. The `docsAvailable` check at line ~77 will now reliably find the docs directory (it's always present in the monorepo, not dependent on sibling checkout).\n   292→\n   293→**Step 2.2: Run `bun run generate-schemas` to verify**\n   294→\n   295→Verify schemas are written to both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n   296→\n   297→### Phase 3: Update strip lists for public sync\n   298→\n   299→**Step 3.1: Update `scripts/sync-public.ts` STRIP_DIRS**\n   300→\n   301→At line 28, add `\"docs\"` to the STRIP_DIRS array:\n   302→```typescript\n   303→const STRIP_DIRS = [\"intermediates\", \"external-docs\", \"public-release-files\", \".github/actions\", \"docs\"];\n   304→```\n   305→\n   306→This ensures the docs workspace doesn't end up in the public runtime snapshot.\n   307→\n   308→**Step 3.2: Update `scripts/release.ts` INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP**\n   309→\n   310→At line 54, add `\"docs/\"` to the strip list:\n   311→```typescript\n   312→const INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP = [\n   313→  \"intermediates/\",\n   314→  \"external-docs/\",\n   315→  \"CLAUDE.md\",\n   316→  \"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\n   317→  \"standard-operating-procedures.md\",\n   318→  \"docs/\",\n   319→];\n   320→```\n   321→\n   322→This ensures the docs workspace is stripped from `release/alpha` during the release process.\n   323→\n   324→**Step 3.3: Update `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` verification list**\n   325→\n   326→At line 160, add `\"docs\"` to the `shouldNotExist` array:\n   327→```typescript\n   328→const shouldNotExist = [\n   329→  \"intermediates\",\n   330→  \"external-docs\",\n   331→  // ... existing entries ...\n   332→  \"docs\",  // Docs workspace should not be in public repo\n   333→];\n   334→```\n   335→\n   336→### Phase 4: Update .gitignore\n   337→\n   338→**Step 4.1: Merge docs-specific ignores into root `.gitignore`**\n   339→\n   340→Add the following to the root `.gitignore` (from `hankweave-docs/.gitignore`):\n   341→\n   342→```gitignore\n   343→# Docs build output\n   344→docs/.next/\n   345→docs/out/\n   346→\n   347→# Pagefind search index (generated at build time)\n   348→docs/public/_pagefind/\n   349→```\n   350→\n   351→Most entries from the docs `.gitignore` (like `node_modules/`, `.env`, `.DS_Store`) are already covered by the root `.gitignore`.\n   352→\n   353→### Phase 5: Update documentation\n   354→\n   355→**Step 5.1: Update `standard-operating-procedures.md` repository structure**\n   356→\n   357→Update the repo structure section (lines 10-30) to reflect the monorepo:\n   358→\n   359→```\n   360→hankweave-dev/              ← private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n   361→├── server/                 ← runtime source code (TypeScript, Bun)\n   362→├── scripts/                ← build, release, sync, and dev tooling\n   363→├── tests/                  ← unit, integration, e2e, cross-runtime\n   364→├── schemas/                ← generated JSON schemas (from Zod)\n   365→├── shims/                  ← agent harness adapters\n   366→├── docs/                   ← documentation site (Next.js + Nextra, Bun workspace)\n   367→│   ├── app/                ← Next.js app directory\n   368→│   ├── content/            ← MDX documentation pages\n   369→│   ├── components/         ← custom React components\n   370→│   ├── public/             ← static assets, schemas, images\n   371→│   └── package.json        ← hankweave-docs workspace\n   372→├── learning/               ← example hanks and guides (ships to public)\n   373→├── intermediates/          ← planning docs, numbered by feature (internal only)\n   374→├── external-docs/          ← SDK reference docs for agent context (internal only)\n   375→├── public-release-files/   ← files overlaid onto the public repo during sync\n   376→├── assets/                 ← images, demo GIFs\n   377→├── .github/                ← CI workflows and composite actions\n   378→├── CHANGELOG.md            ← Keep a Changelog format, [Unreleased] workflow\n   379→├── CONTRIBUTING.md         ← branch model and PR guidelines (internal only)\n   380→└── package.json            ← @southbridgeai/hankweave (private npm) + workspace root\n   381→```\n   382→\n   383→**Step 5.2: Update the \"What gets stripped\" section**\n   384→\n   385→Add `docs/` to the list of stripped directories.\n   386→\n   387→**Step 5.3: Update the schema generation note**\n   388→\n   389→If there's any documentation about the cross-repo schema dependency, update it to note that schemas are now generated directly into `docs/public/schemas/` (same repo).\n   390→\n   391→### Phase 6: Verify everything works\n   392→\n   393→**Step 6.1: Run the full test suite**\n   394→```bash\n   395→bun run lint\n   396→bun run tc\n   397→bun run test:unit\n   398→bun run test:integration\n   399→```\n   400→\n   401→**Step 6.2: Run schema generation**\n   402→```bash\n   403→bun run generate-schemas\n   404→```\n   405→Verify output in both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n   406→\n   407→**Step 6.3: Run the build**\n   408→```bash\n   409→bun run build\n   410→```\n   411→Verify `dist/index.js` is created.\n   412→\n   413→**Step 6.4: Verify docs build**\n   414→```bash\n   415→cd docs && bun run build\n   416→```\n   417→\n   418→**Step 6.5: Test the release dry-run**\n   419→```bash\n   420→bun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks\n   421→```\n   422→Verify validation passes (if on develop with clean tree).\n   423→\n   424→**Step 6.6: Test the sync dry-run**\n   425→```bash\n   426→bun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version <current-version> --use-head\n   427→```\n   428→Verify `docs/` is correctly stripped from the snapshot and the verification checks pass.\n   429→\n   430→### Phase 7: Vercel configuration (out-of-band)\n   431→\n   432→**Step 7.1: Update Vercel project settings**\n   433→\n   434→This is a manual change in the Vercel dashboard, not a code change:\n   435→\n   436→1. Go to the Vercel project for `hankweave-docs`\n   437→2. Go to Settings → General → Root Directory\n   438→3. Change from the current setting (either `/` or `nextra-site/`) to `docs/`\n   439→4. Verify the Framework Preset is still \"Next.js\"\n   440→5. The `vercel.json` inside `docs/` will continue to work\n   441→\n   442→**Step 7.2: Connect Vercel to the monorepo**\n   443→\n   444→If the Vercel project is currently connected to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs`:\n   445→1. Disconnect from `hankweave-docs`\n   446→2. Connect to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`\n   447→3. Set Root Directory to `docs/`\n   448→4. Vercel will deploy when changes are pushed to the configured branch\n   449→\n   450→Note: Vercel can be configured to only deploy when files in the `docs/` directory change, using the \"Ignored Build Step\" setting: `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/`.\n   451→\n   452→### Phase 8: Commit and PR\n   453→\n   454→**Step 8.1: Commit the migration**\n   455→\n   456→Commit all changes as a single atomic commit on the feature branch:\n   457→```\n   458→Migrate to monorepo: bring docs into workspace\n   459→\n   460→- Add docs/ workspace (formerly SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs)\n   461→- Add \"workspaces\" field to root package.json\n   462→- Update generate-schemas.ts to use monorepo-local docs path\n   463→- Add docs/ to strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n   464→- Update .gitignore for docs build artifacts\n   465→- Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n   466→```\n   467→\n   468→**Step 8.2: Open PR targeting develop**\n   469→\n   470→Follow existing PR conventions:\n   471→- Title: `Monorepo migration: consolidate hankweave-docs into workspace`\n   472→- Body: Problem/approach/files format per SOP section 4\n   473→\n   474→---\n   475→\n   476→## g. Testing Considerations\n   477→\n   478→### Existing tests affected\n   479→\n   480→**None of the existing unit, integration, or E2E tests should be affected.** The runtime code is unchanged — no server files, no type files, no config files are modified. Only scripts and metadata files are touched.\n   481→\n   482→The tests that could theoretically be affected:\n   483→\n   484→1. **`tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts`** — Tests that schemas validate correctly. These read from `schemas/` directory which is unchanged.\n   485→2. **E2E init tests** — Test the `--init` scaffolding flow. The runtime code is unchanged so these should pass.\n   486→3. **Any test that reads `package.json`** — The only change is adding a `\"workspaces\"` field, which shouldn't affect anything that reads version, name, or dependencies.\n   487→\n   488→### New tests needed\n   489→\n   490→No new automated tests are strictly required. The migration is a structural change, not a code change. Verification is manual:\n   491→\n   492→1. `bun install` succeeds at root and installs both workspaces\n   493→2. `bun run build` still produces correct dist output\n   494→3. `bun run generate-schemas` writes to both locations\n   495→4. `docs/` build works: `cd docs && bun run build`\n   496→5. Sync dry-run strips `docs/` correctly\n   497→\n   498→### Edge cases to consider\n   499→\n   500→1. **npm publish from root** — `npm publish` uses `\"files\"` field. The `docs/` directory is NOT in the `\"files\"` array (`[\"dist\", \"shims\", \"schemas\"]`), so it won't be included in the npm package. Verify this with `npm pack --dry-run`.\n   501→2. **CI `bun install --frozen-lockfile`** — The new unified `bun.lock` needs to be committed. If it's not, CI will fail because `--frozen-lockfile` doesn't allow lockfile generation.\n   502→3. **`.npmignore` and docs** — The `.npmignore` doesn't need `docs/` added because the `\"files\"` field in `package.json` is an allowlist — only listed paths are included.\n   503→\n   504→---\n   505→\n   506→## h. Documentation Considerations\n   507→\n   508→### Docs to update\n   509→\n   510→1. **`standard-operating-procedures.md`** — Repository structure diagram, strip list documentation (see Phase 5)\n   511→2. **This plan itself** — Should be filed as an intermediate (e.g., `intermediates/45-monorepo-migration/`)\n   512→\n   513→### New docs needed\n   514→\n   515→None required. The monorepo migration is an internal infrastructure change. The docs site content (`docs/content/`) doesn't need updating — it documents Hankweave the product, not the development repo structure.\n   516→\n   517→### Docs that should NOT be updated\n   518→\n   519→- The user-facing docs (`docs/content/guides/getting-started.mdx`, etc.) — these reference `hankweave` as a CLI tool, not as a repo structure\n   520→- The public `README.md` (in `public-release-files/`) — this describes the public `hankweave-runtime` repo, not the private dev repo\n   521→\n   522→---\n   523→\n   524→## i. Additional Resources\n   525→\n   526→### Bun workspaces\n   527→\n   528→- [bun.sh/docs/install/workspaces](https://bun.sh/docs/install/workspaces) — primary reference\n   529→- Root package can be a workspace member itself (important for our \"runtime at root\" approach)\n   530→- `bun install` at root installs all workspace dependencies\n   531→- `bun --filter <name> <script>` runs scripts in specific workspaces (useful for `bun --filter hankweave-docs build`)\n   532→\n   533→### Vercel monorepo support\n   534→\n   535→- Vercel's Root Directory setting specifies which subdirectory contains the deployable project\n   536→- \"Ignored Build Step\" can filter deploys to only docs changes\n   537→\n   538→### Git subtree (optional history preservation)\n   539→\n   540→If docs history is desired:\n   541→```bash\n   542→git remote add -f hankweave-docs <url>\n   543→git merge -s ours --no-commit --allow-unrelated-histories hankweave-docs/main\n   544→git read-tree --prefix=docs/ -u hankweave-docs/main\n   545→git commit -m \"Merge hankweave-docs into monorepo as docs workspace\"\n   546→```\n   547→\n   548→This preserves the full commit history of `hankweave-docs` at the `docs/` prefix. After this, remove the files from `hankweave-docs/` root that aren't needed (README, notes/, plan/) and restructure so the nextra-site contents are at `docs/` root.\n   549→\n   550→Alternatively, a simple file copy with a \"bring docs into monorepo\" commit is simpler and the docs repo's history is available in the original repo if ever needed.\n   551→\n   552→---\n   553→\n   554→## Summary of Changes\n   555→\n   556→| File | Change Type | Description |\n   557→|------|-------------|-------------|\n   558→| `package.json` | Modify | Add `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` |\n   559→| `docs/` | Create (directory) | Contains contents of `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` |\n   560→| `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` | Modify | Update `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path (line 24-32) |\n   561→| `scripts/sync-public.ts` | Modify | Add `\"docs\"` to `STRIP_DIRS` (line 28) |\n   562→| `scripts/release.ts` | Modify | Add `\"docs/\"` to `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` (line 54) |\n   563→| `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` | Modify | Add `\"docs\"` to `shouldNotExist` (line 160) |\n   564→| `.gitignore` | Modify | Add docs build artifacts |\n   565→| `standard-operating-procedures.md` | Modify | Update repo structure diagram |\n   566→| `bun.lock` | Regenerate | New unified lockfile |\n   567→\n   568→**Total files modified**: 7 existing files + 1 new directory of ~30 files\n   569→**Total lines of code changed**: ~20 lines across scripts + SOP update\n   570→\n   571→This is deliberately minimal. The migration's success is measured by how little changes while still achieving the goal: a reliable, explicit relationship between runtime and docs in a single repo.\n   572→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f6abf3a-0b5f-4251-a578-7f2d66ac9b9a","uuid":"9bd97dfe-8207-40fa-a50c-8f9f90945095","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/rough-workspace/opus/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Migrate Hankweave to Monorepo\n\n## a. The Main Task\n\nConsolidate the `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave` (runtime) and `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` (documentation site) repositories into a single monorepo using Bun workspaces. The runtime package stays at the repository root; the docs site moves in as a workspace at `docs/`. The existing CI/CD pipelines, release process, and public sync workflow continue to function with minimal changes.\n\n---\n\n## b. Information Available\n\n### Sources that informed this plan\n\n1. **Task specification** — `plan/task.md` (the task description, open questions, and research)\n2. **Background research** — `plan/background/background.md` (Bun workspace docs, Turborepo evaluation, git subtree options)\n3. **Full source code** — Read every config, script, workflow, and representative server/test files from both repos\n4. **SOP document** — `source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md` (branch model, release process, AI agent policy)\n\n### What I could see\n\n- Full directory structure and file contents of both `source/hankweave/` and `source/hankweave-docs/`\n- All CI workflows, composite actions, and build/release/sync scripts\n- Test infrastructure (patterns, paths, utilities, config fixtures)\n- Both `package.json` files, `tsconfig.json` files, `biome.json`, `bunfig.toml`\n- The docs Nextra/Next.js setup including `vercel.json`, `next.config.mjs`, `app/`, `content/`\n\n### What I could NOT see\n\n- The actual `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` (public mirror) repo — only references to it in scripts and workflows\n- Vercel project settings (the current \"Root Directory\" config for docs deployment)\n- GitHub repo settings (branch protection rules, secrets configuration)\n- Linear project (no ticket ID was provided)\n- Whether there are any other repositories or tools the task spec's \"related packages/tools\" refers to beyond what's in the source snapshot\n\n### Assumptions made\n\n1. The `hankweave-docs` repo has no significant git history worth preserving (the task says \"nice to have\" for history)\n2. The public mirror (`hankweave-runtime`) continues to exist as a separate repo — this migration consolidates the two **private development** repos\n3. The docs site continues to deploy to Vercel from the same repo (now a monorepo)\n4. No Turborepo or other task orchestration is needed for two packages\n\n---\n\n## c. Sources and Related Things\n\n### Original tickets/tasks\n\n- Task description: `plan/task.md`\n- No Linear ticket ID provided\n\n### Code references\n\n| File | Line(s) | Relevance |\n|------|---------|-----------|\n| `source/hankweave/package.json` | Full | Root package.json — needs `workspaces` field added |\n| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/package.json` | Full | Docs package.json — moves to `docs/package.json` |\n| `source/hankweave/scripts/generate-schemas.ts` | 24-32 | The only cross-repo code dependency; path to docs schemas dir |\n| `source/hankweave/scripts/sync-public.ts` | 28-44 | STRIP_DIRS/STRIP_FILES — needs `docs` added to strip list |\n| `source/hankweave/scripts/release.ts` | 54-60 | INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP — needs `docs/` added |\n| `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/ci.yml` | Full | CI workflow — minimal changes needed |\n| `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/release.yml` | Full | Release workflow — minimal changes |\n| `source/hankweave/.github/workflows/sync-public.yml` | Full | Sync workflow — minimal changes |\n| `source/hankweave/.github/actions/setup-environment/action.yml` | Full | Composite action — `bun install` already handles workspaces |\n| `source/hankweave/biome.json` | Full | Linting scope — currently only covers runtime files |\n| `source/hankweave/bunfig.toml` | Full | Bun config — no changes needed |\n| `source/hankweave/tsconfig.json` | Full | Runtime TypeScript config — stays as-is |\n| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/tsconfig.json` | Full | Docs TypeScript config — stays as-is in new location |\n| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/vercel.json` | Full | Vercel config — stays in docs workspace |\n| `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/next.config.mjs` | Full | Next.js config — no changes |\n| `source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md` | 10-30, 34-36 | Repository structure section — needs update |\n| `source/hankweave/.gitignore` | Full | May need additions for docs build artifacts |\n| `source/hankweave/scripts/test-sync-local.ts` | 159-175 | Verification list — needs `docs` added |\n\n### Research sources\n\n- [Bun Workspaces](https://bun.sh/docs/install/workspaces) — native workspace support via `package.json` `workspaces` field\n- [Bun Catalogs](https://bun.sh/docs/install/catalogs) — optional shared dependency versioning (not needed initially)\n- [git subtree merges](https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/using-git/about-git-subtree-merges) — for preserving docs repo history\n\n---\n\n## d. Conventions and Patterns\n\n### Observed code conventions\n\n1. **Scripts are TypeScript** — all build/release/sync scripts are `.ts` files run with `bun`\n2. **Relative paths from `import.meta.dir`** — scripts use `path.join(import.meta.dir, \"..\")` to resolve project root\n3. **`Bun.spawn` for shell commands** — scripts use `Bun.spawn([\"sh\", \"-c\", cmd])` rather than Node's `child_process`\n4. **Two-space indent, 100-char line width** — enforced by Biome\n5. **LF line endings** — enforced by `.gitattributes`\n6. **No shared state between packages** — docs don't import from runtime; only schema files are copied\n7. **Strip lists are explicit** — both `sync-public.ts` and `release.ts` maintain explicit lists of files/dirs to remove\n\n### Patterns to follow\n\n- Add `docs` to existing strip lists rather than creating new mechanisms\n- Keep the root `package.json` as the runtime's package.json (add `workspaces` field only)\n- Don't introduce Turborepo or other tooling — Bun workspaces is sufficient\n- Keep separate `tsconfig.json` per workspace (they have incompatible settings)\n- Don't introduce workspace dependencies (`workspace:*`) between docs and runtime — the schema copy is a script-level operation\n\n### Patterns to avoid\n\n- Don't move the runtime into a subdirectory (would break dozens of paths)\n- Don't create a shared `tsconfig.base.json` (the two configs are too different)\n- Don't add a `bun` workspace filter to CI scripts (just let everything install and run from root)\n\n---\n\n## e. Decision Points and Judgement Calls\n\n### Decision 1: Keep the runtime at the repo root\n\n**Chosen**: The runtime stays at root. The docs site moves into `docs/`.\n\n**Reasoning**: The runtime has 6 scripts, 3 CI workflows, 3 composite actions, build/release/sync pipelines, and extensive relative path usage. Moving it into a subdirectory would require changing every one of these. The docs site has no CI of its own (Vercel builds it), no complex scripts, and one `package.json`. Moving the docs in is a fraction of the work.\n\n**Trade-off**: The root `package.json` serves dual purpose as both workspace root and runtime package. This is a recognized Bun workspace pattern and works correctly — the root package is an \"implicit workspace member\" by default.\n\n**Impact**: Minimal disruption to existing workflows. The main changes are:\n- Adding `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` to root `package.json`\n- Updating 2-3 file paths in scripts\n- Adding `docs` to strip lists\n\n### Decision 2: Flatten the docs repo structure\n\n**Chosen**: Move `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/*` contents directly into `docs/` (not `docs/nextra-site/`).\n\n**Reasoning**: The `nextra-site/` wrapper exists because the docs repo has a root with README, notes, and plan directories. In the monorepo, these don't need a separate layer. The `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `next.config.mjs`, and all source files go directly in `docs/`.\n\n**Alternative considered**: Keeping `docs/nextra-site/` as-is. This preserves the original structure but adds an unnecessary level of nesting. It also means `\"workspaces\": [\"docs/nextra-site\"]` which is less clean.\n\n**What to do with `hankweave-docs/` non-nextra files**: The `README.md` at docs repo root, `notes/`, and `plan/` directories are development artifacts. They can either:\n- Be discarded (they're internal planning docs)\n- Be moved to an `intermediates/` entry documenting the docs site\n- Be kept at `docs/` level alongside the nextra files\n\n**Recommendation**: Discard `notes/` and `plan/` (they're historical planning docs). Keep the `README.md` as `docs/README.md` if desired, but it's not required.\n\n### Decision 3: Don't use `workspace:*` dependencies\n\n**Chosen**: No workspace dependency between docs and runtime.\n\n**Reasoning**: The docs site doesn't import from the runtime. The only data flow is schema JSON files copied by `generate-schemas.ts`. This is a script-level file copy, not a package dependency. Adding a `workspace:*` dependency would incorrectly suggest the docs depend on the runtime as a package.\n\n**When to revisit**: If the docs site ever needs to import TypeScript types or utilities from the runtime (e.g., for auto-generated API reference), add `workspace:*` at that point.\n\n### Decision 4: Convert the existing hankweave repo, don't create new\n\n**Chosen**: Modify `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave` in-place to become the monorepo.\n\n**Reasoning**: All CI workflows, GitHub secrets, branch protection rules, Linear integration, and team permissions are already configured on this repo. Creating a new repo would require reconfiguring everything. The existing git history stays intact. The docs files are brought in via a merge commit (or `git subtree add` if history preservation is desired).\n\n**Impact**: No disruption to existing CI/CD. No need to update secrets, protections, or integrations.\n\n### Decision 5: No Turborepo\n\n**Chosen**: Use Bun workspaces alone, no Turborepo.\n\n**Reasoning**: Two packages don't need task orchestration or caching. The runtime builds and tests independently. The docs site builds independently on Vercel. There's no dependency chain requiring `^build` semantics. Adding Turborepo would increase complexity with no clear benefit.\n\n**When to revisit**: If more packages are added (e.g., a shared types package, a CLI package), or if CI times become a problem and caching would help.\n\n### Decision 6: Single lockfile at root\n\n**Chosen**: One `bun.lock` at the repo root, replacing both existing lockfiles.\n\n**Reasoning**: Bun workspaces uses a single root lockfile. Both workspace packages' dependencies are resolved and locked together. This is how Bun workspaces work by default — there's no option for per-workspace lockfiles.\n\n**Impact**: The `bun.lock` from `hankweave` and the `bun.lock` from `hankweave-docs/nextra-site` are both replaced by a regenerated root `bun.lock`. The first `bun install` after migration will generate this.\n\n### Over/under engineering line\n\n- **Under**: Not adding path filtering to CI (docs changes trigger runtime tests). Acceptable for now — CI runs are fast and infrequent enough.\n- **Under**: Not using Bun catalogs for shared TypeScript version. Acceptable — the projects only share TypeScript and it's fine to have independent versions.\n- **Over**: Adding Turborepo, shared configs, workspace link scripts, or monorepo-specific CI tooling. Not needed for two packages.\n- **Right level**: Adding `docs` to strip lists, updating one path in `generate-schemas.ts`, updating the SOP doc. Minimal changes that make the monorepo work.\n\n---\n\n## f. The Actual Implementation Plan\n\n### Phase 0: Preparation\n\n**Step 0.1: Create a feature branch**\n```bash\ngit checkout develop\ngit pull origin develop\ngit checkout -b hrishi/monorepo-migration  # or similar\n```\n\n**Step 0.2: Verify clean state**\n- Ensure all tests pass: `bun run test:unit`, `bun run lint`, `bun run tc`\n- Ensure working directory is clean: `git status`\n\n### Phase 1: Bring docs into the repo\n\n**Step 1.1: Create the `docs/` directory**\n\nCopy the contents of `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/` at the runtime repo root.\n\nFiles to copy from `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/`:\n```\napp/\ncomponents/\ncontent/\npublic/\nstyles/\nbun.lock           (will be removed later — root lockfile takes over)\nmdx-components.tsx\nnext-env.d.ts\nnext.config.mjs\npackage.json\ntsconfig.json\nvercel.json\n```\n\nFiles from `hankweave-docs/` root to optionally include:\n```\n.gitignore          → merge relevant rules into root .gitignore\nREADME.md           → can include as docs/README.md (internal docs readme)\n```\n\nFiles to NOT copy:\n```\nnotes/              → historical planning docs, discard\nplan/               → historical planning docs, discard\n```\n\n**Step 1.2: Add workspace configuration to root `package.json`**\n\nModify `source/hankweave/package.json` — add `workspaces` field:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"@southbridgeai/hankweave\",\n  \"version\": \"0.5.6\",\n  \"workspaces\": [\"docs\"],\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n**Step 1.3: Delete the docs-side `bun.lock`**\n\nRemove `docs/bun.lock` (the old `nextra-site/bun.lock`). The root lockfile will manage all dependencies.\n\n**Step 1.4: Run `bun install`**\n\nFrom the repo root, run `bun install`. This:\n- Resolves dependencies for both workspaces\n- Generates a new unified `bun.lock` at root\n- Creates a single `node_modules/` tree\n\nVerify: `docs/node_modules` should be a symlink or the workspace should be hoisted.\n\n**Step 1.5: Verify docs build locally**\n\n```bash\ncd docs && bun run build\n```\n\nVerify the Next.js build succeeds. If there are issues with module resolution, they'll surface here.\n\n### Phase 2: Update cross-repo references\n\n**Step 2.1: Update `scripts/generate-schemas.ts`**\n\nChange the `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path from:\n```typescript\nconst DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR = path.join(\n  import.meta.dir,\n  \"..\",\n  \"..\",\n  \"hankweave-docs\",\n  \"nextra-site\",\n  \"public\",\n  \"schemas\",\n);\n```\n\nTo:\n```typescript\nconst DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR = path.join(\n  import.meta.dir,\n  \"..\",\n  \"docs\",\n  \"public\",\n  \"schemas\",\n);\n```\n\nThis is the only code change needed to formalize the cross-package dependency. The `docsAvailable` check at line ~77 will now reliably find the docs directory (it's always present in the monorepo, not dependent on sibling checkout).\n\n**Step 2.2: Run `bun run generate-schemas` to verify**\n\nVerify schemas are written to both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n\n### Phase 3: Update strip lists for public sync\n\n**Step 3.1: Update `scripts/sync-public.ts` STRIP_DIRS**\n\nAt line 28, add `\"docs\"` to the STRIP_DIRS array:\n```typescript\nconst STRIP_DIRS = [\"intermediates\", \"external-docs\", \"public-release-files\", \".github/actions\", \"docs\"];\n```\n\nThis ensures the docs workspace doesn't end up in the public runtime snapshot.\n\n**Step 3.2: Update `scripts/release.ts` INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP**\n\nAt line 54, add `\"docs/\"` to the strip list:\n```typescript\nconst INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP = [\n  \"intermediates/\",\n  \"external-docs/\",\n  \"CLAUDE.md\",\n  \"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\n  \"standard-operating-procedures.md\",\n  \"docs/\",\n];\n```\n\nThis ensures the docs workspace is stripped from `release/alpha` during the release process.\n\n**Step 3.3: Update `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` verification list**\n\nAt line 160, add `\"docs\"` to the `shouldNotExist` array:\n```typescript\nconst shouldNotExist = [\n  \"intermediates\",\n  \"external-docs\",\n  // ... existing entries ...\n  \"docs\",  // Docs workspace should not be in public repo\n];\n```\n\n### Phase 4: Update .gitignore\n\n**Step 4.1: Merge docs-specific ignores into root `.gitignore`**\n\nAdd the following to the root `.gitignore` (from `hankweave-docs/.gitignore`):\n\n```gitignore\n# Docs build output\ndocs/.next/\ndocs/out/\n\n# Pagefind search index (generated at build time)\ndocs/public/_pagefind/\n```\n\nMost entries from the docs `.gitignore` (like `node_modules/`, `.env`, `.DS_Store`) are already covered by the root `.gitignore`.\n\n### Phase 5: Update documentation\n\n**Step 5.1: Update `standard-operating-procedures.md` repository structure**\n\nUpdate the repo structure section (lines 10-30) to reflect the monorepo:\n\n```\nhankweave-dev/              ← private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n├── server/                 ← runtime source code (TypeScript, Bun)\n├── scripts/                ← build, release, sync, and dev tooling\n├── tests/                  ← unit, integration, e2e, cross-runtime\n├── schemas/                ← generated JSON schemas (from Zod)\n├── shims/                  ← agent harness adapters\n├── docs/                   ← documentation site (Next.js + Nextra, Bun workspace)\n│   ├── app/                ← Next.js app directory\n│   ├── content/            ← MDX documentation pages\n│   ├── components/         ← custom React components\n│   ├── public/             ← static assets, schemas, images\n│   └── package.json        ← hankweave-docs workspace\n├── learning/               ← example hanks and guides (ships to public)\n├── intermediates/          ← planning docs, numbered by feature (internal only)\n├── external-docs/          ← SDK reference docs for agent context (internal only)\n├── public-release-files/   ← files overlaid onto the public repo during sync\n├── assets/                 ← images, demo GIFs\n├── .github/                ← CI workflows and composite actions\n├── CHANGELOG.md            ← Keep a Changelog format, [Unreleased] workflow\n├── CONTRIBUTING.md         ← branch model and PR guidelines (internal only)\n└── package.json            ← @southbridgeai/hankweave (private npm) + workspace root\n```\n\n**Step 5.2: Update the \"What gets stripped\" section**\n\nAdd `docs/` to the list of stripped directories.\n\n**Step 5.3: Update the schema generation note**\n\nIf there's any documentation about the cross-repo schema dependency, update it to note that schemas are now generated directly into `docs/public/schemas/` (same repo).\n\n### Phase 6: Verify everything works\n\n**Step 6.1: Run the full test suite**\n```bash\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\nbun run test:unit\nbun run test:integration\n```\n\n**Step 6.2: Run schema generation**\n```bash\nbun run generate-schemas\n```\nVerify output in both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n\n**Step 6.3: Run the build**\n```bash\nbun run build\n```\nVerify `dist/index.js` is created.\n\n**Step 6.4: Verify docs build**\n```bash\ncd docs && bun run build\n```\n\n**Step 6.5: Test the release dry-run**\n```bash\nbun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks\n```\nVerify validation passes (if on develop with clean tree).\n\n**Step 6.6: Test the sync dry-run**\n```bash\nbun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version <current-version> --use-head\n```\nVerify `docs/` is correctly stripped from the snapshot and the verification checks pass.\n\n### Phase 7: Vercel configuration (out-of-band)\n\n**Step 7.1: Update Vercel project settings**\n\nThis is a manual change in the Vercel dashboard, not a code change:\n\n1. Go to the Vercel project for `hankweave-docs`\n2. Go to Settings → General → Root Directory\n3. Change from the current setting (either `/` or `nextra-site/`) to `docs/`\n4. Verify the Framework Preset is still \"Next.js\"\n5. The `vercel.json` inside `docs/` will continue to work\n\n**Step 7.2: Connect Vercel to the monorepo**\n\nIf the Vercel project is currently connected to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs`:\n1. Disconnect from `hankweave-docs`\n2. Connect to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`\n3. Set Root Directory to `docs/`\n4. Vercel will deploy when changes are pushed to the configured branch\n\nNote: Vercel can be configured to only deploy when files in the `docs/` directory change, using the \"Ignored Build Step\" setting: `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/`.\n\n### Phase 8: Commit and PR\n\n**Step 8.1: Commit the migration**\n\nCommit all changes as a single atomic commit on the feature branch:\n```\nMigrate to monorepo: bring docs into workspace\n\n- Add docs/ workspace (formerly SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs)\n- Add \"workspaces\" field to root package.json\n- Update generate-schemas.ts to use monorepo-local docs path\n- Add docs/ to strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n- Update .gitignore for docs build artifacts\n- Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n```\n\n**Step 8.2: Open PR targeting develop**\n\nFollow existing PR conventions:\n- Title: `Monorepo migration: consolidate hankweave-docs into workspace`\n- Body: Problem/approach/files format per SOP section 4\n\n---\n\n## g. Testing Considerations\n\n### Existing tests affected\n\n**None of the existing unit, integration, or E2E tests should be affected.** The runtime code is unchanged — no server files, no type files, no config files are modified. Only scripts and metadata files are touched.\n\nThe tests that could theoretically be affected:\n\n1. **`tests/unit/json-schema.test.ts`** — Tests that schemas validate correctly. These read from `schemas/` directory which is unchanged.\n2. **E2E init tests** — Test the `--init` scaffolding flow. The runtime code is unchanged so these should pass.\n3. **Any test that reads `package.json`** — The only change is adding a `\"workspaces\"` field, which shouldn't affect anything that reads version, name, or dependencies.\n\n### New tests needed\n\nNo new automated tests are strictly required. The migration is a structural change, not a code change. Verification is manual:\n\n1. `bun install` succeeds at root and installs both workspaces\n2. `bun run build` still produces correct dist output\n3. `bun run generate-schemas` writes to both locations\n4. `docs/` build works: `cd docs && bun run build`\n5. Sync dry-run strips `docs/` correctly\n\n### Edge cases to consider\n\n1. **npm publish from root** — `npm publish` uses `\"files\"` field. The `docs/` directory is NOT in the `\"files\"` array (`[\"dist\", \"shims\", \"schemas\"]`), so it won't be included in the npm package. Verify this with `npm pack --dry-run`.\n2. **CI `bun install --frozen-lockfile`** — The new unified `bun.lock` needs to be committed. If it's not, CI will fail because `--frozen-lockfile` doesn't allow lockfile generation.\n3. **`.npmignore` and docs** — The `.npmignore` doesn't need `docs/` added because the `\"files\"` field in `package.json` is an allowlist — only listed paths are included.\n\n---\n\n## h. Documentation Considerations\n\n### Docs to update\n\n1. **`standard-operating-procedures.md`** — Repository structure diagram, strip list documentation (see Phase 5)\n2. **This plan itself** — Should be filed as an intermediate (e.g., `intermediates/45-monorepo-migration/`)\n\n### New docs needed\n\nNone required. The monorepo migration is an internal infrastructure change. The docs site content (`docs/content/`) doesn't need updating — it documents Hankweave the product, not the development repo structure.\n\n### Docs that should NOT be updated\n\n- The user-facing docs (`docs/content/guides/getting-started.mdx`, etc.) — these reference `hankweave` as a CLI tool, not as a repo structure\n- The public `README.md` (in `public-release-files/`) — this describes the public `hankweave-runtime` repo, not the private dev repo\n\n---\n\n## i. Additional Resources\n\n### Bun workspaces\n\n- [bun.sh/docs/install/workspaces](https://bun.sh/docs/install/workspaces) — primary reference\n- Root package can be a workspace member itself (important for our \"runtime at root\" approach)\n- `bun install` at root installs all workspace dependencies\n- `bun --filter <name> <script>` runs scripts in specific workspaces (useful for `bun --filter hankweave-docs build`)\n\n### Vercel monorepo support\n\n- Vercel's Root Directory setting specifies which subdirectory contains the deployable project\n- \"Ignored Build Step\" can filter deploys to only docs changes\n\n### Git subtree (optional history preservation)\n\nIf docs history is desired:\n```bash\ngit remote add -f hankweave-docs <url>\ngit merge -s ours --no-commit --allow-unrelated-histories hankweave-docs/main\ngit read-tree --prefix=docs/ -u hankweave-docs/main\ngit commit -m \"Merge hankweave-docs into monorepo as docs workspace\"\n```\n\nThis preserves the full commit history of `hankweave-docs` at the `docs/` prefix. After this, remove the files from `hankweave-docs/` root that aren't needed (README, notes/, plan/) and restructure so the nextra-site contents are at `docs/` root.\n\nAlternatively, a simple file copy with a \"bring docs into monorepo\" commit is simpler and the docs repo's history is available in the original repo if ever needed.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n| File | Change Type | Description |\n|------|-------------|-------------|\n| `package.json` | Modify | Add `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` |\n| `docs/` | Create (directory) | Contains contents of `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` |\n| `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` | Modify | Update `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path (line 24-32) |\n| `scripts/sync-public.ts` | Modify | Add `\"docs\"` to `STRIP_DIRS` (line 28) |\n| `scripts/release.ts` | Modify | Add `\"docs/\"` to `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` (line 54) |\n| `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` | Modify | Add `\"docs\"` to `shouldNotExist` (line 160) |\n| `.gitignore` | Modify | Add docs build artifacts |\n| `standard-operating-procedures.md` | Modify | Update repo structure diagram |\n| `bun.lock` | Regenerate | New unified lockfile |\n\n**Total files modified**: 7 existing files + 1 new directory of ~30 files\n**Total lines of code changed**: ~20 lines across scripts + SOP update\n\nThis is deliberately minimal. The migration's success is measured by how little changes while still achieving the goal: a reliable, explicit relationship between runtime and docs in a single repo.\n","numLines":572,"startLine":1,"totalLines":572}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:21:00.049Z"}
